I chose Spring Boot mainly because it allows me to build scalable and production-ready backend applications with clean architecture.

It provides features like auto-configuration and dependency injection, which helped me focus more on business logic instead of setup.

Also, Spring Boot integrates well with Spring Security, which made it easier for me to implement JWT-based authentication and role-based access control in my project.

Additionally, its support for REST API development and database integration using JPA and Hibernate helped me design a structured backend system efficiently.

Overall, it gave me a complete ecosystem to build and manage real-world applications.




👉 “Why not Node.js / Django?”

Say:

I considered other frameworks, but I chose Spring Boot because of its strong support for structured enterprise applications, built-in security features, and better alignment with Java, which I use for DSA and backend development.
